From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:32:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] qwen3_5: the mHC kernels under the shared contract
 gates, with FP64 references
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

contract_q35_mhc.zig registers tf_q35_mhc_{branch,merge,enter,leave} with a planted
control each: the host reference is the same definition in FP64 — row-normalised
streams, 20 log-space Sinkhorn passes, branch = pre . streams, streams =
mix @ streams + post * branch, and the entry folding the pending output. The group
loads the mHC image and resolves the four handles itself, so the runner's one line
is register().

Also: the plan accessors refuse a geometry that carries no valid loop (cuda_disk_test
built one field by field and attentions() underflowed), TF_Q35_DEBUG has its
environment_test coverage row, and linear_attn.norm reads an HF checkpoint's f32.
